{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cp /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/tmp/w3/assurance_generated_test.go /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/assurance_generated_test.go && cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && cat > update-08.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Continued on the open necessary gap for the five-node reachability history: by which path the diverged peer was reconciled. The harness now emits a per-node timeline (state, term, last, applied, store bounds) plus the peer's Restore count and applied-command count immediately after the heal and at 200/400/700/1000/1300 ms. Local construction feedback already shows something the previous receipt could not: at the first sample the successor's snapshot had been installed by the old leader while the peer was reconciled from store 1..7 to store 1..4 with zero restores, so the repair path is still unidentified and is not a snapshot install. The successor harness is registered so this becomes retained evidence.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 220, \\\"end_line\\\": 300, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl-snap8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 299, \\\"end_line\\\": 375, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-installsnap8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"raft.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1814, \\\"end_line\\\": 1953, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-lastindex8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"state.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 157, \\\"end_line\\\": 174, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-compact8\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"snapshot.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 216, \\\"end_line\\\": 262, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@q-reachability-history\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"By which path is a diverged peer reconciled when the current leader's own log store has been fully compacted, and which node supplies the entries that replace its stale suffix?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-repl8\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap8\\\", \\\"src-installsnap8\\\", \\\"src-lastindex8\\\", \\\"src-compact8\\\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"gaps\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-reachability-history\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Which node sent the AppendEntries that replaced the peer's stale suffix in the five-node history, and does that path exist only because a different node had already installed the successor's snapshot (which would leave it holding lastLogIndex above lastSnapshotIndex with only the post-snapshot logs retained)?\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-reachability-history\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-repl8\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap8\\\", \\\"src-installsnap8\\\", \\\"src-lastindex8\\\", \\\"src-compact8\\\"],\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recorded against the retained receipt CheckRun b9b56ddf3d7d43319db460b87846f71f and the local timeline feedback from the successor harness. What the retained receipt already showed: the peer held earlier-term entries beyond the successor's snapshot index (divergent_prefix index 0), the successor's store was fully compacted (successor_snapshot index 1, store first/last 0) and the peer was reconciled to store 1..4 with applied index 4 and zero FSM restores (rejoin_observe index 2). Local timeline feedback adds the shape of that reconciliation: immediately after the heal the successor was still leader at term 3 with store 0/0, three nodes sat at store 1..4 with applied 4, and one node - the previously partitioned leader - sat at store 5..7 with last 7, applied 4 and term 3, i.e. that node had installed the successor's snapshot (lastSnapshotIndex 4) while its stale suffix 5..7 remained and its lastLogIndex stayed 7. So the peer's repair is not a snapshot install and not attributable to the successor's log store; the state of the previously partitioned leader also reproduces, on the follower side, exactly the mismatch the single-peer witness showed on the leader side (advertised last entry above the snapshot index whose term is the older term). This remains unresolved: neither the retained receipt nor the timeline identifies the sender or the exact AppendEntries sequence, so no claim is made about it. It also keeps the earlier narrowing in force - the leader-side loop is asserted only within its executed single-peer basis.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The peer converged without any InstallSnapshot (restores 0) although the successor's log store was empty, so a compaction-and-snapshot-only explanation of its repair is refuted.\\\",\n        \\\"The previously partitioned leader retained store 5..7 with lastLogIndex 7 and lastSnapshotIndex 4 after installing the successor's snapshot, so having installed a snapshot does not by itself reset the advertised last entry.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"Source-only conclusion in this batch: the timeline harness has not been executed by the controller yet, so the timeline numbers are non-retained construction feedback.\\\",\n        \\\"The harness does not instrument RPC traffic, so the sender of the repairing AppendEntries cannot be read directly from the observations; only node states, applied-command counts and store bounds are visible.\\\",\n        \\\"One configuration and one process; other timeout and trailing-log settings were not sampled.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"experiment\\\": {\n    \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-reachability-history\\\",\n    \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n    \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-repl8\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap8\\\", \\\"src-installsnap8\\\", \\\"src-lastindex8\\\", \\\"src-compact8\\\"],\n    \\\"scope\\\": {\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Same five-node legal history as the previous harness (isolate the leader from three peers, let it replicate uncommitted commands to one peer, let the majority side elect a successor that snapshots inside the peer's stale suffix, then heal), extended with a per-node timeline sampled immediately after the heal and at 200/400/700/1000/1300 ms: leadership, state, term, last index, applied index and log-store bounds for every node, plus the peer's FSM Restore count and applied-command count.\\\",\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n        \\\"The timeline is sufficient to attribute the repair to a snapshot install or to AppendEntries by comparing each node's store bounds and applied index against the peer's.\\\",\n        \\\"Counting Restore calls per FSM identifies snapshot installs without touching production logic.\\\",\n        \\\"The precondition guard skips rather than fails when an election does not complete in time, so a run without the precondition yields no observation.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"excluded\\\": [\n        \\\"No RPC-level instrumentation and no network transport; the sender of a repairing AppendEntries is inferred from node state, not read from the wire.\\\",\n        \\\"The single-peer loop witness is not re-executed here.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"parameters\\\": { \\\"peers\\\": 5, \\\"uncommitted_commands\\\": 5, \\\"timeline_ms\\\": [0, 200, 400, 700, 1000, 1300] }\n    },\n    \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"MakeClusterCustom(Peers=5, Bootstrap=true, Conf{TrailingLogs:0, SnapshotInterval:1h, SnapshotThreshold:1<<20, HeartbeatTimeout/ElectionTimeout/LeaderLeaseTimeout:1s, CommitTimeout:10ms}, MakeFSMFunc returning a Restore-counting MockFSM). Wait for a leader; partner=followers[0], others=the remaining three; disconnect leader<->other both ways; base=leader.LastIndex(); fire five leader.Apply calls and wait until partner.LastIndex()>base, emitting divergent_prefix with both sides' last index, the partner's store bounds and the divergence index. Wait up to 12s for a successor among others; apply one command; Snapshot(); emit successor_snapshot with snapshot index/term, successor term, its last and applied index and store bounds. Then FullyConnect() and, for ms in {0,200,400,700,1000,1300}, emit timeline with the current leader, each node's state/term/last/applied/store bounds and the partner's Restore count and applied-command count; finally emit rejoin_observe with the restore counts and the partner's and successor's indexes and store bounds.\\\",\n    \\\"responsibility\\\": \\\"A repair claim must be attributable to an identified producer and path; a node holding stale entries above a snapshot boundary must be shown to lose them, not assumed to.\\\"\n  }\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-08.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
